    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Section 3 mandates that no person shall drive a motor vehicle in any public place without a valid driving license.",
        "Section 4 establishes the legal age limits for driving, setting 18 years for motor vehicles and 20 years for transport vehicles.",
        "Section 185 outlines strict penalties, including fines and imprisonment, for driving under the influence of alcohol or drugs.",
        "Section 128 and Section 194D mandate the use of protective headgear (helmets) for two-wheeler drivers and pillion riders.",
        "Section 130 requires drivers to produce their driving license, registration certificate, and insurance documents upon demand by an authorized officer."
      ],
      "id": "f6i6g8z"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Section 185 (Drunken Driving): Frequently tested regarding the legal limit of 30 mg of alcohol per 100 ml of blood detected by a breath analyser.",
        "Section 181 vs Section 180: Section 181 penalizes driving without a license, whereas Section 180 penalizes the owner for allowing an unauthorized person to drive.",
        "Section 194B & 194D: High-frequency questions on revised 2019 amendment penalties for non-use of seatbelts and helmets."
      ],
      "id": "vfysv99"
    },
